  "entry": "code/primer.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). From a genomic sequence with exons in UPPERCASE and introns in lowercase, design primer3 primer pairs whose amplicons span each exon-exon junction, so genomic DNA is not amplified. Pairs are ranked by penalty and dimer ΔG, the binding sites are mapped on the sequence, and a summary of the top-recommended pair can be downloaded before checking it in NCBI Primer-BLAST. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
